# RX-02 creator-crash qualification
PR: https://github.com/applicate2628/mcp-local-hub/pull/625
Head:
8698d24e622253b8d9e2d1bd96d29fb97e5de4f1
Base: bfff5699d893199f4c18d15add2a39e801e94a78

## Scope
Five new native cases verify the preexisting owner after successful process creation: suspended root; live root/one descendant; root code7 with live descendant; explicit context/stdio route; normal finish control.
Only test executable, integration test and README changed. Runtime library/API/manifest/lock remain byte-identical to base.
Observer retains native process handles verified by source fixture PID+creationtime+image before owner termination, never an observer Job handle. Owner is terminated through its own original Child handle. Independent control remains alive.
Outcomes are captured before owned safety cleanup. Drop witness distinguishes Rust unwinding from abrupt termination; native waits prove observed exits. No generic process census, no PID-only production authority.

## Evidence
Initial qualification passed. Disabling only KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE: three abrupt cases failed while normal finish passed; separate explicit-context/stdio case failed. All mutated runtime bytes restored, tests repeated.
Final full experimental crate:39 native integration +3 unit +2 compile-fail doctests. Three debug runs, one release run, plus exact-source debug after review comment. No ignored/filtered test cases in full runs.
Clippy -Dwarnings, fmt check and git diff-check passed. Windows11 build26100/x86_64/Rust1.99.1, offline locked cached dependencies. No Unix runtime/cross-build or new target installation.
No missing-image one-time handle-growth explanation established; prior uncertainty remains documented.

## Remaining
In-progress acquisition/native create/resume/close fault cases, actual blocking IO cancellation, noninheritable stdio conversion, Go/Rust ABI and foreign caller, native Unix, equal-contract Go comparison, independent review and product integration.
Crash-tested points are post-create only; no power-loss, arbitrary escape/schedules, remote outcome rollback or exhaustive durability proof.
Full remaining R01-R24 status updated in existing plan PR#623, not a new status file in product.

## Preservation
Everything new under D:\dev\ChatGPT. The exact original windows.rs backup was confirmed equal to base/current and moved to approved trash, not deleted. Logs, fixtures, hashes and needed source remain outside trash.
Remote branch and local source matched; worktree clean. No production installation/config/active-main/other code branches touched. No merge, paid/model/provider or explicit bot/CI launch.
===== END RESULTS.md =====

